Ladybird keeps an automatic content-derived abspos height indefinite
for child percentage sizing, even when it calculates that height before
inside layout. Stretch and orthogonal-flow sizes remain definite, as
do sizes transferred through a definite preferred aspect ratio.

Blink rejects fit-content heights in CanComputeBlockSizeWithoutLayout(),
and ComputeOofBlockDimensions() lays out the content without setting a
fixed block size. Gecko leaves the automatic block size unconstrained
in nsIFrame::ComputeAbsolutePosAutoSize() for an automatic block inset.

WebKit leaves that height unresolved in RenderBlock::
availableLogicalHeightForPercentageComputation(), while handling
explicit, aspect-ratio, and fully constrained heights separately.
Ladybird matches those engines for content-sized abspos flex containers
with auto block insets. Chrome measurements confirm that a 50%-height
item with 60px of content stays 60px tall in a wrapping column flexbox.
